# Expectation record for 14_abi_calling_convention/005_struct_return_by_value.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 005_struct_return_by_value
area               = 14_abi_calling_convention
description        = Aggregates returned by value across the same size thresholds: an 8-byte, four 16-byte layouts, a 24-byte and a 40-byte struct, each returned twice, plus a returned aggregate consumed directly as a member access and one forwarded straight into another call, in a folded and a volatile-runtime variant
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour by construction:
- Every floating value is a dyadic rational exactly representable in binary32 and binary64
  alike, printed with an explicit precision with room to spare, so no rounding decision is
  taken and i686's x87 extended intermediate precision cannot perturb a result. Each float
  member is cast to double explicitly where it is printed. No non-finite value, no negative
  zero and no division appears.
- No signed integer overflow. The 40-byte producer's loop adds a loop counter bounded by 10
  to a base of at most 7200, and every other member is a small literal or a snapshot.
- No shift operator appears, so no shift count can be out of range.
- PADDING DISCIPLINE. sizeof is never printed and no aggregate is ever memcmp'd or inspected
  byte-wise; only NAMED MEMBERS are read back, so no padding byte is ever read and the
  per-target layout of the mixed aggregate cannot affect the output.
- Every array index is a bounded loop counter or a constant strictly inside bounds, so no
  one-past-end pointer is formed and none is dereferenced. The four snapshot loops each run
  exactly as many iterations as their source array has elements.
- No aliasing violation: every aggregate is returned by value and copied whole between
  objects of the same type, never through a converted pointer.
- No read of uninitialized storage: each producer assigns every member of its result before
  returning it, and every staged local is assigned before use.
- No object is modified twice between sequence points.
- Reading a member directly off a call expression -- one of the three consumption paths --
  is well defined: the returned value is an object with temporary lifetime and the member
  access happens within that lifetime, in the same full expression.
- NOTHING DEPENDS ON UNSPECIFIED EVALUATION ORDER, and this is enforced structurally
  rather than argued. An access to a volatile object IS an observable side effect, and
  C11 6.5.2.2p10 leaves the order of evaluation of a call's FUNCTION DESIGNATOR, of its
  arguments, and of subexpressions within those arguments unspecified. Two shapes in this
  program would therefore have been unsound, and both are structurally absent:
    - reading one volatile object more than once inside a single argument list, which the
      direct member probes would do if they read a maker's volatile pointer once per member
      (two reads for the 8-byte shape, six for the 24-byte one); and
    - reading two volatile objects in one full expression, which a forwarding call would do
      if it read the consumer's pointer as its designator and the maker's pointer inside its
      argument.
  Neither can arise, because NO VOLATILE LVALUE APPEARS ANYWHERE IN main BEYOND ITS OWN
  SNAPSHOT STATEMENT. Every volatile datum -- the sixteen ints, the six doubles, the eight
  floats, the twelve 24-byte-shape ints and all FOURTEEN call-boundary function pointers --
  is read exactly once, in a statement of its own, and only the resulting plain locals are
  used thereafter. Machine-checked on this branch: flattening the program into statements
  and counting references to its volatile objects finds NO statement with more than one.
  The snapshots cost nothing in coverage. A staged value is still a value that arrived
  through a volatile load, so the optimizer may neither fold nor elide it and every callee
  still receives arguments genuinely materialised at run time; and a function pointer whose
  value arrived through a volatile load still designates a function no conforming compiler
  can identify, so every call through it is still indirect, still un-inlined and still
  un-cloned. Verified in the generated assembly: at -O2 on x86_64 and aarch64 all seven
  producers and all seven consumers are emitted unmodified, with no .constprop and no .isra
  clone. What changed is only that the loads are now SEQUENCED rather than unordered.
- Hermetic, as constraint C4 requires: every input is a literal in the source. Nothing is
  opened, no socket is created, no environment variable and no program argument is read,
  and no storage is obtained from the heap.
- main returns 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires.
- Verified empirically on this branch: the default strict warning gate
  (-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror) produces zero
  diagnostics at -O0, -O1 and -O2, and -fsanitize=undefined,address
  -fno-sanitize-recover=all runs to completion with empty stderr and exit status 0.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
WHY RETURN IS A SEPARATE MECHANISM FROM PASSING on every one of the four supported ABIs,
which is why this program exists alongside 004: an 8-byte aggregate comes back in one
general-purpose register on the 64-bit targets; a 16-byte all-integer aggregate in a
register pair, the exact boundary; the mixed int-and-double aggregate in rax + xmm0 on
System V AMD64, x0 + x1 on AAPCS64 and a0 + fa0 on LP64D, which is the highest-yield return
shape in the corpus; a two-double aggregate in xmm0 + xmm1 on AMD64, as a homogeneous
floating aggregate on AAPCS64 and in fa0 + fa1 on LP64D; a four-float aggregate as an
AAPCS64 homogeneous aggregate return, two packed SSE registers on AMD64 and a
general-purpose pair on LP64D; and the 24-byte and 40-byte aggregates through a hidden
pointer everywhere. System V i386 cdecl returns every aggregate through a caller-supplied
hidden pointer, which is a fifth distinct mechanism.

THREE CONSUMPTION PATHS are exercised for each variant, because they can lower differently:
storing the returned aggregate in a local and reading its members, reading a member
directly off the call expression without storing it, and forwarding the returned aggregate
straight into another function as an argument.

COVERAGE OF THE BY-MEMORY SHAPE. For the 40-byte aggregate every one of the ten members is
read back rather than a sample of three, because a return path that corrupted only an
interior member would otherwise leave no trace in stdout.

THE CALL BARRIER, AND WHERE THE POINTER IS READ. Every call this program makes to the
function whose ABI boundary is under test goes through a FILE-SCOPE volatile FUNCTION
POINTER, and that is load-bearing rather than stylistic. A C11 volatile lvalue must be
re-read on every access, so no conforming compiler may assume which function the pointer
designates: it can neither inline the callee nor clone it, and it must marshal the
arguments exactly as the ABI prescribes because it cannot know what will receive them.
This is plain standard C rather than a compiler attribute, so both sides of oracle (a)
honour it for the same reason and neither needs to support an extension for the barrier to
hold.

The volatile pointer is read ONCE PER RUN, at the top of main, into a plain local function
pointer, and every call site uses that local. That placement is deliberate and it is what
keeps the one-volatile-access-per-full-expression rule satisfied without weakening the
barrier: the local's value came from a volatile load, so it is still opaque to the
compiler, while a call site that re-read the volatile object would place one or two
observable side effects inside an argument list whose evaluation order C11 6.5.2.2p10
leaves unspecified. Reading it at the call site would buy nothing -- the barrier is a
property of where the value CAME FROM, not of how often it is fetched -- and would cost the
program its own defined behaviour, which is the precondition every oracle here rests on.
Measured before-state on this branch: with direct calls, gcc 13.4.0 at
-O2 left only make_sbig standing -- every small, mixed and homogeneous-float return and both
forwarding consumers were inlined away, so six of the seven documented return mechanisms and
both forwarding paths were not exercised at that level. Measured after: all seven producers
and both consumers are emitted unmodified at -O1 and -O2 on all four targets, with no
.constprop and no .isra clone anywhere.

Plain char signedness is implementation-defined and was measured as signed on x86_64 and
i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64; no plain-char value is printed. sizeof(long) and
sizeof(void *) were measured as 4 on i686 and 8 on x86_64, aarch64 and riscv64
(docs/technical-specifications.md lines 457-462); no long, size_t, ptrdiff_t, intptr_t or
pointer value is printed and no long or pointer conversion specification is used. long
double has three different representations across the four targets (measured 16, 12, 16 and
16 bytes; x87 80-bit versus IEEE binary128) and is absent from this program entirely --
using it would import a difference that has nothing to do with parameter passing. That
type is covered by 13_floating_point/004_long_double_target_restricted, whose record
disables oracle (b) alone, with the measured reason recorded and the expected-divergence
marker XD-TYPE-LONGDOUBLE-001 scoping that oracle.

No target is dropped, no oracle is disabled and this record carries no expected-divergence
marker: a cross-backend divergence here is a GENUINE FINDING rather than an
implementation-defined difference, because nothing implementation-defined reaches the
output. Measured on this branch with gcc 13.4.0 and the matching i686, aarch64 and riscv64
cross drivers, executed natively and under QEMU user-mode 10.1.0: stdout is byte-identical
and the exit status is 0 in all twelve target-and-optimization-level cells.
END
